  "response_text": "the kernel contains the core functions of the operating system\u2014like scheduling, context switching, and managing hardware access. These are implemented in kernel.c and related files. The user, on the other hand, writes application code (such as thread functions or main programs), which lives in separate files like main.c. This separation is important because it isolates privileged operations in the kernel, preventing user code from accidentally or maliciously modifying core system behavior. From the user\u2019s perspective, this structure makes the system easier to use, safer, and more modular. The user writes their application logic without needing to understand or alter how the OS itself works.\\n",
